Depends.  In the early game, he's not too hard to play since 
he's the pet-master (the stethoscope and his healing spells 
keeps them alive; you can even have one horse clear out mine 
town if you keep an eye on it's HP), plus he knows of potions 
of * healing.  His starting equipment can easily be used, if you 
find an early altar, to boost your HP.  After the castle, he's 
similar to the rest, but his great Quest item gives him an 
edge.  The thing which takes some skill or luck is the 
mid-game when your pet can't protect you from everything 
any longer; if you don't have some decent armor class then, 
you're in trouble.  (That's why I tend to dive in the mines 
as soon as I find them, just to find some dwarven mithril.  
Then I'm out of it again.)  I found it harder to ascend a 
tourist; however, I couldn't ascend a barbarian yet, so 
maybe it's just my strange playing style.  

